---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

---
<BaseLayout title="How to Enable DNSSEC in Cloudflare" description="Enable DNSSEC in Cloudflare step by step: get the DS record, publish it at your registrar, and verify the chain of trust."  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["DNS Guide", "/dns/"], ["Enable DNSSEC in Cloudflare"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Enable DNSSEC in Cloudflare</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Enable DNSSEC in Cloudflare</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      Cloudflare signs your zone automatically; your half of the job is publishing the DS record at
      your registrar. Get the order right and the whole thing is a five-minute toggle.
    </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">DNSSEC activation in Cloudflare</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Verification</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">1. Enable signing</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">DNS settings, Enable DNSSEC</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Cloudflare signs the zone instantly</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">2. Publish the DS record</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">One-click to supported registrars, or copy the DS to the registrar</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">DS visible at the parent zone</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">3. Confirm the chain</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">DS + DNSKEY visible, validation green</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Our DNSSEC checker validates end to end</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#step-by-step">Step by step</a></li>
        <li><a href="#the-one-warning-that-matters">The one warning that matters</a></li>
        <li><a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 id="step-by-step">Step by step</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Open DNS settings</strong> in the Cloudflare dashboard for your domain and scroll to DNSSEC. Click Enable.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy the DS record</strong> Cloudflare displays: key tag, algorithm (13), digest type (2), and the digest. Cloudflare also shows registrar-specific instructions for major registrars.</li>
        <li><strong>Publish the DS at your registrar</strong> (where you bought the domain, not where DNS is hosted). Most registrars have an "Add DS record" flow under domain settings; some import it from the parent automatically once you paste the tuple.</li>
        <li><strong>Wait for propagation</strong>, up to a few hours for the parent zone to serve the new DS.</li>
        <li><strong>Verify the chain</strong>: our <a href="/dns-record-lookup/">record lookup</a> with DS selected should return the record, and your site should resolve normally through validating resolvers (Quad9, Cloudflare's own 1.1.1.1).</li>
        <li><strong>Watch the dashboard status</strong> move to Active. If it stays "Pending", the registrar side hasn't landed.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="the-one-warning-that-matters">The one warning that matters</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare handles key rotation for you. If you ever move DNS away from Cloudflare,
        <strong>disable DNSSEC and wait out the DS TTL before switching nameservers</strong>: a
        parent DS pointing at servers that no longer sign your zone is the classic domain-wide
        SERVFAIL. See <a href="/what-is-dnssec/">what is DNSSEC</a> for the full mechanism.
      </p>
      <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><em>Stuck on pending:</em> the DS at the registrar is missing a field or mangled; re-copy the tuple.</li>
        <li><em>SERVFAIL after enabling:</em> almost always digest mismatch; compare the DS at the parent with the one Cloudflare shows.</li>
        <li><em>Registrar without DS support:</em> rare now, but transfer to one that supports DNSSEC delegation.</li>
      </ul>
      
<h2 id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/ds-record/">DS records</a> and <a href="/dnskey-record/">DNSKEY records</a></li>
        <li><a href="/what-is-dnssec/">What is DNSSEC?</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does Cloudflare DNSSEC cost anything?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. DNSSEC signing is included on all plans, and Cloudflare can publish the DS record to supported registrars in one click.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does DNSSEC activation take?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Signing is near-instant on Cloudflare; the DS record at the registrar propagates within minutes to hours. Validation goes green once the chain is visible.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What if my registrar does not support DS records?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Then the chain of trust cannot complete and DNSSEC stays inactive for that domain. Move DNS delegation to a registrar that publishes DS records, or host DNS with the registrar that does.</p></details></div>
      </div>
</BaseLayout>
